.TH "GENI\-UPLOADER\-PLAN" "1" "October 2026" "geni-uploader 1.0.0" "Geni Uploader Manual"
.SH NAME
geni\-uploader\-plan \- dry\-run a manifest against live Geni state without writing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geni\-uploader plan
.BI "\-\-manifest " "MANIFEST"
.BI "[\-\-log " "LOG]"
.BI "[\-\-state " "STATE]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Loads the manifest, checks every referenced file, fetches each profile and its document/photo listings with GET requests only, verifies the expected names, and reports which items would upload and which would be skipped as already present.
.PP
No writes to Geni, to the state file, or to the repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-token\-file " "TOKEN_FILE"
file outside the repo holding the access token (global, before the command)
.TP
.BI "\-\-manifest " "MANIFEST"
path to the upload manifest file (required)
.TP
.BI "\-\-log " "LOG"
diagnostic log file (run default: geni\-upload\-run.log next to the state file; plan default: stdout only)
.TP
.BI "\-\-state " "STATE"
durable state file path (default: geni\-upload\-state.json)
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short summary and the option list, then exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B geni\-uploader plan \-\-manifest packages/batch\-01/upload\-manifest.yaml
Show what would upload, writing nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the command completed
.TP
.B 1
failure (see the diagnostic log)
.TP
.B 2
refused (for example a missing \-\-confirm YES)
.TP
.B 3
uncertain items remain; review them on Geni before re\-running
.TP
.B 4
identity or tag verification stopped the run
.TP
.B 5
uploads are verified on Geni; only the repository status push failed
.TP
.B 6
another run holds the state lock
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR geni\-uploader (1).
